{
  "_readme": [
    "The branch structure of the encounter-resolution graph, r300-r343.",
    "",
    "Hand-written and tracked, like errata.json, procedures.json and",
    "creatures.json: this records the *shape* of each section - which stat is",
    "checked, against which comparison, and which of the eight primitives each",
    "branch lands on. It restates none of the booklet's text, and it is useless",
    "without data/sections.json beside it, which is generated and not tracked.",
    "See docs/plans/00-overview.md open question Q1.",
    "",
    "Sections whose outcomes were extracted into data/tables.json are marked",
    "shape 'inline_table' and read from there rather than repeated here.",
    "Sections that need real logic are marked shape 'handler' and live in",
    "src/engine/rules/graph.py.",
    "",
    "  shape check       1d6 against a party stat; branches to pass/fail",
    "  shape bribe       pay the amount the calling section supplied, or fail",
    "  shape fight/escape/hide/pass    a terminal, no roll",
    "  shape inline_table  resolve via data/tables.json (it carries the gotos)",
    "  shape outcome_table a die table whose rows carry more than a target",
    "  shape handler     explicit Python",
    "",
    "  stat  wits | party_size      party_size is living men, not mounts",
    "  op    ge | gt | lt | le      wits ge means wit & wiles >= the die",
    "",
    "  do    fight | escape | hide | pass | battle | retry | goto | join",
    "",
    "initiative maps to a combat setup: 'us'/'them' say who strikes first, and",
    "surprise names the side granted the free bonus strike (r220d)."
  ],

  "sections": {
    "r300": {"cite": "r300", "shape": "fight", "initiative": "us", "surprise": "us"},

    "r301": {"cite": "r301", "shape": "check", "stat": "wits", "op": "ge",
             "pass": {"do": "fight", "initiative": "us", "surprise": "us"},
             "fail": {"do": "fight", "initiative": "us"}},
    "r302": {"cite": "r302", "shape": "check", "stat": "wits", "op": "gt",
